 "confidence": "high",
 "notes": "Hand-lettered sheet, one 15-pin connector, 'REAR VIEW OF CONNECTOR', 'CONNECTOR TYPE: ELCO # 00-6007-015-940-002'. The drawing names no connector, so it is called P1. Left bracket: 'INPUT WHEN USED AS PROGRAM AMP' ties to pins 4 and 6. Right bracket: 'INPUT WHEN USED AS SUMMING AMP (N/A FOR M450A)' ties to pins 3 and 5, so on the M450A only 4/6 is the input. No +/- polarity drawn on inputs or OUTPUT (12/13), so ports use 'a'/'b'. INPUT SHIELD 7 is assumed to belong to the program input (the drawing just says INPUT SHIELD). Title block: Ward-Beck Systems Ltd., 450-04-001, size A, ISS. 2, DRN. GEB, DATE JUNE 76 (file name says 1973), CKD. signed. No insert."
